    <!-- Lead -->
    <p class="lead">Most product descriptions fail before a shopper finishes the first sentence — not because the product is bad, but because the copy treats features like benefits, buries the value proposition, and reads like a spec sheet. AI can fix this. But only if you prompt it correctly.</p>

    <p>Generic prompts produce generic descriptions. "Write a product description for a yoga mat" gives you something usable. The right conversion-focused prompt gives you something that makes people add to cart.</p>
